What is a Security Agreement?

A Security Agreement is a legal document used to secure a loan by giving the lender a legal interest in the borrower's personal property as collateral. If the borrower fails to repay the debt, the lender may claim or recover value from the pledged property according to the agreement terms.

Collateral may include vehicles, machinery, inventory, jewelry, equipment, electronics, collectibles, or other valuable personal assets.

Why Use a Security Agreement?

Using a professionally drafted Security Agreement helps:
• Protect the lender from non-payment
• Secure a loan with valuable collateral
• Define borrower obligations clearly
• Reduce disputes over pledged assets
• Provide legal proof of security interest
• Increase chances of loan approval
• Strengthen private lending arrangements

